{"slug":"ops-prod-ops","title":"Production operations","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Production environment (canonical)"},{"id":"b2","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Fact"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Value"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Host"}],[{"type":"text","value":"89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — Hetzner cax11, ARM64 (aarch64), Ubuntu 22.04"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"App dir"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (server tracks "},{"type":"text","value":"origin/main","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"core.hooksPath=.githooks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Service"}],[{"type":"text","value":"systemd "},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark.service","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; wrapper "},{"type":"text","value":"api/start.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (sources ASDF + "},{"type":"text","value":".env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Proxy"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Caddy on :80 → "},{"type":"text","value":"localhost:4000","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"/etc/caddy/Caddyfile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Erlang/Elixir"}],[{"type":"text","value":"via ASDF (Erlang Solutions has no ARM packages)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Go"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/usr/local/go/bin/go","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (official ARM64 binary)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Env file"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark/.env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"DATABASE_URL","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"SECRET_KEY_BASE","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_EXTRA_ORIGINS","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ws origins)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Logs"}],[{"type":"text","value":"journalctl -u barkpark -f","marks":["code"]}]]]},{"id":"b3","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Deploy: "},{"type":"text","value":"ssh root@89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"cd /opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"git pull","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (post-merge hook auto-rebuilds + restarts) or "},{"type":"text","value":"make deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Golden Rules apply verbatim — never partial-clean "},{"type":"text","value":"_build","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", never skip "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", always test after deploy."}]},{"id":"b4","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The postcheck rule"},{"id":"b5","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A misbooted or stopped Phoenix node looks identical to a healthy one from outside the box — systemd returned, SSH closed, no error surfaced. So any workflow that touches "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on production "},{"type":"text","value":"must","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" end with "},{"type":"text","value":"api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", which probes the public HTTP surface."}]},{"id":"b6","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Atomic transitions:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" prefer "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" over stop-then-start; a deliberate stop without restart gets documented before you run it."}],[{"type":"text","value":"No silent ops:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" SSH'd in to patch something? Run the script before you log out. The point is to refuse \"looks fine, didn't check.\""}]]},{"id":"b7","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"How to run"},{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"From a workstation:"}]},{"id":"b9","type":"code","value":"ssh root@<prod-host> \"cd /opt/barkpark && ./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh\""},{"id":"b10","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"On the box itself:"}]},{"id":"b11","type":"code","value":"cd /opt/barkpark\n./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh"},{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Exit code 0 = healthy. Non-zero = unhealthy; the script writes a tail of "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl status barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to stderr before exiting so you have an immediate diagnostic without a second SSH round-trip."}]},{"id":"b13","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"What it checks"},{"id":"b14","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Service is active.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl is-active --quiet barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". If the unit is inactive the script starts it — the script is a recovery guardrail, not a passive monitor. Run it only when \"service should be running\" is the desired end state."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Boot delay.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Sleeps 2 s before the HTTP probe so the BEAM has time to bind "},{"type":"text","value":":4000","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" after a fresh start."}],[{"type":"text","value":"HTTP 200 from ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"/api/schemas","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":".","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Legacy unauth path. Returns JSON when Phoenix is alive, no auth header required. Probe path can be swapped to "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (HTML 200) if the legacy schemas endpoint is ever retired; do not swap to "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/schemas/production","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (admin-token gated)."}]]},{"id":"b15","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Operational checklist"},{"id":"b16","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Apply the change via the documented Makefile target ("},{"type":"text","value":"make deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"make rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"make restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") rather than ad-hoc "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" invocations where possible."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"text","value":"./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Confirm "},{"type":"text","value":"PASS prod healthy …","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Tail "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl -u barkpark -f","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" for at least 60 s and watch for boot errors, repeated supervisor restarts, or 5xx-emitting controllers."}],[{"type":"text","value":"If the postcheck FAILs: read the "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" tail it printed, then "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl -u barkpark -n 200 --no-pager","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" for the surrounding context. Do not retry the same "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" invocation blindly."}]]},{"id":"b17","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Prod migrations — validated live 2026-06-10 (95-commit deploy, 5 migrations)"},{"id":"b18","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The post-merge hook compiles and restarts but does "},{"type":"text","value":"NOT","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" run migrations. Additive migrations (the normal case): migrate FIRST — old code ignores new columns, but new code selecting an unmigrated column 500s on every request:"}]},{"id":"b19","type":"code","value":"ssh root@89.167.28.206 && cd /opt/barkpark\nset -a; . ./.env; set +a                    # backup: ecto:// -> postgresql://\npg_dump \"${DATABASE_URL/ecto:/postgresql:}\" | gzip > /root/pre-deploy.sql.gz\ngit checkout -- bin/barkpark go.mod         # build-dirtied artifacts abort the pull\ngit -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null pull --ff-only   # NO hook — old code keeps serving\nmake migrate                                # bash start.sh mix ecto.migrate (ASDF + .env)\nbash .githooks/post-merge                   # clean rebuild + restart\n./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh"},{"id":"b20","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Destructive migrations (drop/rename) have no zero-downtime order — schedule a window: stop, migrate, deploy, start."}]},{"id":"b21","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Known transient: in the rebuild window, error-path requests on the old BEAM can crash ("},{"type":"text","value":"Plug.Exception is undefined","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — lazy-loading from the deleted "},{"type":"text","value":"_build","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). Self-heals at restart; deploy in quiet moments, don't chase it."}]},{"id":"b22","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Never run "},{"type":"text","value":"make reset-db","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (drop + recreate) or "},{"type":"text","value":"mix ecto.reset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on production. If a migration fails mid-way, stop — read "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl -u barkpark -n 200","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", do not retry blindly, and prefer a forward-fix migration over editing an applied one."}]},{"id":"b23","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Phoenix server rollback"},{"id":"b24","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Roll back by reverting source, never by resetting the server checkout:"}]},{"id":"b25","type":"code","value":"# On a workstation (ask before pushing, per repo rules):\ngit revert <bad-sha>          # forward-moving revert commit on main\ngit push\n\n# On the server:\nssh root@89.167.28.206\ncd /opt/barkpark\ngit pull                      # post-merge hook rebuilds + restarts\n# or explicitly: make deploy  (git pull + full clean rebuild + restart)\n./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh"},{"id":"b26","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Rules: never "},{"type":"text","value":"git reset --hard","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or force-push on the prod checkout; the rebuild must be the full "},{"type":"text","value":"make rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" clean path (nuke "},{"type":"text","value":"api/_build/prod","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") — a partial clean serves stale BEAM/HEEx (Past Mistakes #1–3). If the bad commit included a migration, rolling back code does NOT undo the schema; write a compensating migration if the schema change itself must be undone. npm/SDK rollback is a separate runbook: ops-npm-rollback-playbook."}]},{"id":"b27","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Code anchors"},{"id":"b28","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — the postcheck script"}],[{"type":"text","value":".githooks/post-merge","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — auto-rebuild on server "},{"type":"text","value":"git pull","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (no migrate step)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Makefile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"text","value":"rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"migrate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" targets"}],[{"type":"text","value":"api/start.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — systemd wrapper sourcing ASDF + "},{"type":"text","value":".env","marks":["code"]}]]}],"related":["ops-npm-rollback-playbook"]}
